cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If ns-sdn contributes to published work, cite the IEEE-ORSS paper the package implements (preferred-citation), the FLAIRS paper that introduced the architecture (references), and the software itself."
type: software
title: "ns-sdn: the Non-Stationary Spectral Decomposition Network"
abstract: "A neural state-space model that represents a scalar time series as a trend plus a small number of sinusoids whose amplitude, instantaneous frequency, phase offset and participation evolve with a latent state, fitted as a one-step forecaster and read as an interpretable time-varying spectral decomposition with spectral-state coordinates."
